#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""gpu-yield: keep a local LLM loaded while a Bazzite gaming PC is idle, and get it
out of the GPU's way the moment a game starts.

  No game running  -> Ollama runs with the model preloaded in VRAM.
  Game starts      -> Ollama is stopped immediately. A stand-in answers on the same
                      port with "503 GPU busy" so remote clients (Hermes) know why.
  Game exits       -> after a cooldown, Ollama starts and the model is reloaded.

Games are detected through Steam's `reaper` helper, which Steam uses to launch every
game in its library (including non-Steam shortcuts), so no per-game setup is needed.

Commands:
  gpu-yield setup       install Ollama (user-level), this tool and its services
  gpu-yield status      what is happening right now
  gpu-yield model       choose or change the model (downloads it)
  gpu-yield restart     unload the model, free GPU memory, load it again
  gpu-yield pause       keep the AI off until `resume` (survives reboots)
  gpu-yield resume
  gpu-yield doctor      check the whole setup
  gpu-yield update      update from GitHub (--check to look, --ollama to update Ollama too,
                        --file PATH to install a local copy instead)
  gpu-yield rollback    go back to the version before the last update
  gpu-yield uninstall   remove services (add --purge to remove Ollama and config)
  gpu-yield run         the watcher itself; systemd runs this

Logs:  journalctl --user -u gpu-yield -u gpu-yield-ollama -f
"""

